; S-06 intent_match field projections
;
; Six tiny Forms covering two record types:
;   Intent       : intent_budget, acceptance_form
;   MatchResult  : match_kind, none_reason, fulfiller_hash, sub_attention_id
;
; Same pattern as s04-projections.form: STORE arg, READ, READSLOT
; to the schema-helper layer ("Intent/proj/*" / "MatchResult/proj/*"),
; CALL, RET.
;
; Synthesis chain (abbreviated — projection is a leaf):
;   provocation:  STUBS.md catalogues these six S-06 projections as
;                 pending. S-06's body (S-06-intent-match.form) calls
;                 them via READSLOT name + CALL.
;   grounding:    A1.2 (type is intrinsic), A6.1 (a unit of code is
;                 a substance), A0.6 (code is thought, not artifact).
;   composes_with: schema sub-helpers under "Intent/proj/*" and
;                  "MatchResult/proj/*" — catalogued in STUBS.md as
;                  Schema/* primitives once their substance layouts
;                  are written in kernel/types/SCHEMA.md (the Intent
;                  and MatchResult sections are scheduled for the
;                  next SCHEMA.md batch). Until those land, these
;                  projection bodies have a pending leaf at the
;                  inner CALL — consistent with the v0.2.0-helpers
;                  layered approach established by s04-projections.

; ============================================================
; S-06/proj/intent_budget — extract intent.budget
; ============================================================

(form
  :type-tag      "Form/v1"
  :name          "S06_proj_intent_budget"
  :declared-caps (S-03/ROOT_RO)
  :declared-traps (ETYPE)
  :arity         1
  :locals-n      2
  :code (
    STORE   0
    LOAD    0
    READ
    STORE   1
    LOAD    1
    PUSH    "Intent/proj/budget"
    SEAL    Hash
    READSLOT
    CALL    h=$ /n=1
    RET
  )
  :rationale-hash $$BLAKE3$$/s06-projections-rationale
)

